DESCRIPTION:This session focuses on the preservation and stewardship of or
 al histories once interviews are complete. Archivists will introduce parti
 cipants to archival workflows at Brown University and the John Hay Library
 \, including preservation formats\, access considerations\, and ethical re
 sponsibilities. The workshop emphasizes how thoughtful preservation ensure
 s oral histories remain accessible and meaningful for future generations. 
 No prior experience with archives\, oral history\, or historical research 
 is necessary. All three sessions must be attended to receive an Oral Histo
 ry Certificate.\nCategory: Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal lis
