DESCRIPTION:In_CORPUS is a performative intervention conceived by Agnès L
 ópez-Río specifically for Carlos Aires’s installation Bailad\, bailad
 \, malditos \, in Nave 0 at Matadero Madrid. Through dance\, the piece est
 ablishes a dialogue with the exhibition’s visual and sonic universe\, as
  well as with Sydney Pollack’s They Shoot Horses\, Don’t They? (1969)
 —a shared cinematic reference from which both Carlos Aires and Agnès L
 ópez-Río explore the relationships between the body\, the image\, and sp
 ectacle. Performed by Agnès López-Río and Isaac Montllor\, the action u
 nfolds among the props of the installation\, where movement\, repetition\,
  and breath build a physical experience moving between the energy of dance
  and t\nCategory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.matader
 omadrid.org/en/schedule/incorpus
LOCATION:Nave 0\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
